===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*nebʰ-}}
From {{der|en|la|Neptūnius|t=of or pertaining to the Roman god Neptune}}, from {{m|la|Neptūnus|t=the Roman god Neptune}} (possibly ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*nebʰ-|t=to become damp, cloudy}}) + {{m|la|-ius|pos=''suffix forming {{glossary|adjective}}s from {{glossary|noun}}s''}}; analysable as {{suffix|en|Neptune|ian}}. The English word is cognate with {{cog|fr|neptunien|t=pertaining to the Roman god Neptune, pertaining to the sea, pertaining to Neptunism, Neptunian; proponent of Neptunism, Neptunist}}, {{cog|de|Neptunier|t=proponent of Neptunism, Neptunist}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n.'' and ''adj|id=126156|date=September 2003|nodot=yes}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj}}</ref>

