# {{lb|en|astrology}} A person under the [[astrological]] [[influence#Noun|influence]] of the [[planet]] Neptune.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Shakuntala Devi|chapter=Characteristics of the Planets|title=Astrology for You|location=New Delhi|publisher=Orient Paperbacks|year=1983|year_published=2007|page=54|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=acUbv_gjVcEC&pg=PA54|isbn=978-81-222-0067-6|passage=To a '''Neptunian''' the common satisfaction of life seems too banal, and he often seeks the hidden mysteries of life. The advanced soul however realises that life is a dream, and a divine dream at that.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Liz Greene|chapter=Neptune and the Artist|title=The Astrological Neptune and the Quest for Redemption|edition=1st paperback|location=York Beach, Me.|publisher=[[w:Red Wheel/Weiser/Conari|Samuel Weiser, Inc.]]|year=2000|page=324|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=Zo77spK78yoC&pg=PA324|isbn=978-1-57863-197-1|passage=Often the '''Neptunian''' cannot bring his or her fantasies to birth in form because the fantasy world remains a surrogate womb, static rather than flowing, a place of painless oblivion rather than a bridge between human and divine.}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|science fiction}} An ([[imaginary]]) [[inhabitant]] of the [[planet]] [[Neptune]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Camille Flammarion|chapter=The Planet Neptune and the Frontiers of the Solar Domain|translator=[[w:John Ellard Gore|J[ohn] Ellard Gore]]|title=Popular Astronomy: A General Description of the Heavens: [...] Translated from the French with the Author’s Sanction|location=London|publisher={{w|Chatto & Windus}},{{nb...|Piccadilly}}|year=1894|page=470|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/popularastronom00flamgoog/page/n497/mode/1up|oclc=7927688|passage=I need not say that from Neptune the earth is completely invisible, as well as Mercury, Venus, and Jupiter. Saturn is a little star which departs from the sun up to 18°. For the '''Neptunians''' the solar system appears to be composed of the sun, Saturn, Uranus, their own world, and the planet which doubtless gravitates beyond Neptune.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:John Russell Fearn|chapter=12|title=Quorne Returns|series=The Golden Amazon Saga|seriesvolume=book 6|location=[Rockville, Md.]|publisher=w:Wildside Press|year=1952|year_published=2013|page=102|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=saX0AAAAQBAJ&pg=PA102|isbn=978-1-4794-0989-1|passage=We learn the energy quotient of a bogus Earthling, note how much it varies from that of a genuine one, and then proceed to carefully single out every '''Neptunian'''. It will take time, no doubt, but not perhaps as long as we think, as the percentage of '''Neptunians''' to Earthlings is small.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Justin McCory Martin|chapter=March|title=Marvelous Month-by-month Writing Prompts: 250 Knock-their-socks-off Writing Prompts to Inspire Super Writing All Year Long!|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Scholastic Corporation|Scholastic Professional Books]]|year=2001|page=43|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=w0PEjlWbP-EC&pg=PP45|isbn=978-0-439-22250-1|passage=Pretend that you are a visitor to Earth from the planet Neptune. When you return home you will want to describe Earthlings to your fellow '''Neptunians'''. [...] Good luck! Or as '''Neptunians''' say, "Urk bliff!"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Patricia Ann Pich|chapter=Neptune|title=Out of this World: A Fairy Tale for Children of All Ages|location=[Bloomington, Ind.]|publisher=[[w:AuthorHouse|1stBooks]]|date=12 April 2001|pages=5–6|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=BK1o-YK9sP4C&pg=PA5|isbn=978-0-7596-2308-8|passage=Since Neptune had been the chosen planet to help Earth work through its current series of crises, '''Neptunians''' were key beings at this time. Each visit to Earth was a specific mission for those who were chosen to travel there.}}

